{
  "case_id": "2017-15-1485",
  "document_hash": "648838ec3f3478642d0bf4af03bc8b2303fa9520beadc56048791167e46fcb54",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Todd Kim",
      "case_id": "2017-15-1485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "648838ec3f3478642d0bf4af03bc8b2303fa9520beadc56048791167e46fcb54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-648838ec3f34-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Probable cause is a practical standard, and thus it accounts for the practical limitations that officers face when making arrest decisions, including their inability to look directly into the minds of suspects offering innocent explanations for suspicious conduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-15-1485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "648838ec3f3478642d0bf4af03bc8b2303fa9520beadc56048791167e46fcb54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-648838ec3f34-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Kim, before you do that, could you clarify the other charges that are in this case, the one relating to disorderly conduct and negligent supervision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Robert A. Parker",
      "case_id": "2017-15-1485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "648838ec3f3478642d0bf4af03bc8b2303fa9520beadc56048791167e46fcb54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-648838ec3f34-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are two fundamental errors in the way that the lower courts analyzed the question of probable cause in this case. First, they took certain important facts out of context, viewed them in isolation, and engaged in precisely the sort of divide-and-conquer analysis that this Court has said is inappropriate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-15-1485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "648838ec3f3478642d0bf4af03bc8b2303fa9520beadc56048791167e46fcb54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-648838ec3f34-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: You are saying that anytime a policeman goes into a house and there's a party and people tell you, somebody invited me, and it turns out that that somebody didn't have a right to be in the house, you can arrest them?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-15-1485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "648838ec3f3478642d0bf4af03bc8b2303fa9520beadc56048791167e46fcb54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-648838ec3f34-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One might ask what other evidence they could have looked for. One of -- Justice Alito asked, what else could they have done?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2017-15-1485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "648838ec3f3478642d0bf4af03bc8b2303fa9520beadc56048791167e46fcb54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-648838ec3f34-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that these officers were plainly incompetent in disregarding"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2017-15-1485",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "648838ec3f3478642d0bf4af03bc8b2303fa9520beadc56048791167e46fcb54",
      "evidence_id": "ev-648838ec3f34-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As to whether or not this -- the question of competing motions for summary judgment is properly before the Court at this point, it's not just that they didn't raise the disputes. They affirmatively said in their brief in opposition this is the factual background."
    },
    {
